@startuml AWS ALB - Detailed Sequence Diagram

!theme plain
title AWS ALB - Request Processing Flow (Production - Current Architecture)

actor User
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant "Internet\nGateway" as IGW
participant "Application\nLoad Balancer" as ALB
participant "Auth Service\n(ECS Fargate)" as Auth
database "RDS\nPostgreSQL" as DB

== User Request ==

User -> Browser: Click "View Profile"
Browser -> IGW: GET /api/auth/profile\nAuthorization: Bearer eyJhbGc...

== AWS Network ==

IGW -> ALB: Forward request
note right
    Public subnet
    Port: 80
end note

ALB -> ALB: Match listener rule
note right
    **Listener Rules:**
    
    Priority 10: /api/auth*
    → Auth Target Group
    → ECS Tasks (Port 3001)
    
    ⚠️ NO processing
    ⚠️ Just routing
end note

ALB -> ALB: Health check
note right
    Target Group health status:
    ✅ Healthy targets: 1
    
    Forward to: 10.0.1.45:3001
end note

== Forward to ECS ==

ALB -> Auth: Forward request\n(Private subnet)
note right
    GET http://10.0.1.45:3001/api/auth/profile
    
    **Headers (unchanged):**
    Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIs...
    
    ❌ NO x-user-* headers
    ❌ NO x-api-gateway-secret
    ❌ NO processing at all
end note

== Service Must Do Everything ==

Auth -> Auth: ❌ validateApiGatewaySecret
note right
    const secret = req.headers['x-api-gateway-secret'];
    
    ❌ secret = undefined
    
    **Problem:**
    Can't verify if request came through ALB
    or direct access to service
    
    **Solution:**
    Skip this check OR use VPC security groups
end note

Auth -> Auth: Manual JWT verification
note right
    **Step 1: Extract token**
    const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;
    const token = authHeader?.replace('Bearer ', '');
    
    ❌ Must parse manually
end note

Auth -> Auth: Verify JWT signature
note right
    **Step 2: Load public key**
    const publicKey = fs.readFileSync('public.pem');
    
    **Step 3: Verify**
    jwt.verify(token, publicKey, {
        algorithms: ['RS256']
    });
    
    ❌ CPU intensive (RSA verification)
    ⚠️ ~10-15ms per request
end note

Auth -> Auth: Check expiration
note right
    **Step 4: Decode payload**
    const decoded = jwt.decode(token);
    
    **Step 5: Check exp**
    if (decoded.exp * 1000 < Date.now()) {
        throw new Error('Token expired');
    }
    
    ❌ Must implement manually
end note

Auth -> Auth: Extract user claims
note right
    **Step 6: Attach to request**
    req.user = {
        id: decoded.id,
        email: decoded.email,
        role: decoded.role,
        full_name: decoded.full_name
    };
    
    ❌ Every service duplicates this logic
end note

Auth -> Auth: Business logic
note right
    const userId = req.user.id;
    const email = req.user.email;
    
    ✅ Finally can process request
end note

Auth -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE id = '507f1f77bcf86cd799439011'
note right
    RDS endpoint:
    club-auth-db.abc.ap-southeast-1.rds.amazonaws.com
    
    Connection through private subnet
end note

DB -> Auth: User data

Auth -> Auth: Build response
note right
    {
      "id": "507f1f77bcf86cd799439011",
      "email": "john@example.com",
      "full_name": "John Doe",
      "role": "user",
      "created_at": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    }
end note

== Response ==

Auth -> ALB: 200 OK\n+ User Profile JSON

ALB -> IGW: Forward response

IGW -> Browser: 200 OK\n+ User Profile JSON

Browser -> User: Display Profile

== Timing & Issues ==

note over ALB, Auth
    **Performance Breakdown:**
    
    1. ALB routing: ~5ms
    2. Forward to ECS: ~3ms
    3. JWT verification (service): ~15ms ❌
    4. Claims extraction (service): ~2ms ❌
    5. Business logic: ~20ms
    
    **Total: ~45ms**
    
    **BUT every service pays JWT overhead!**
end note

note over Auth
    **Problems with Current Approach:**
    
    ❌ **Code Duplication**
       - JWT verification in EVERY service
       - Auth, Club, Event, Image, Notify
       - 5x duplicate code
    
    ❌ **Security Concerns**
       - Can't verify request source
       - Services exposed to direct access
       - No centralized policy
    
    ❌ **Maintenance**
       - Update JWT logic in 5 places
       - Inconsistent implementations
       - Hard to audit
    
    ❌ **Performance**
       - Each service does RSA verification
       - 5x CPU overhead
       - No caching between services
    
    ⚠️ **No API Gateway Features**
       - No rate limiting
       - No request transformation
       - No circuit breaker
       - No centralized logging
end note

== Alternative: With Kong on AWS ==

note over ALB, Auth #LightBlue
    **If we deploy Kong on ECS:**
    
    Internet → ALB → Kong (ECS) → Services
    
    **Benefits:**
    ✅ JWT verified once at Kong
    ✅ Services get clean headers
    ✅ API Gateway Secret works
    ✅ Consistent with local dev
    ✅ Centralized security
    
    **Cost:**
    ~$25/month for Kong container
    +20-30ms latency
    
    **Trade-off:**
    Worth it for >10M requests/month
end note

@enduml
